# Local XYZ Euler poses keep articulation data separate from world placements.
import scene_transforms.dl

class:
    patterns:
        UI scene pose
    members:
        position as UI scene vector
        rotation as UI scene vector
        scale as UI scene vector

to get [a UI scene vector from] {a value:components}:
    require condition ((the length of components) = 3) reporting "Scene vectors require three components"
    return a new vector with x ((the item at 0 in components) as a 64 bit floating-point number), y ((the item at 1 in components) as a 64 bit floating-point number) and z ((the item at 2 in components) as a 64 bit floating-point number)

to [require finite UI scene vector] {vector:value}:
    set converted to the UI scene vector form of value
    require condition (((the x of converted) is finite) and (((the y of converted) is finite) and ((the z of converted) is finite))) reporting "Scene pose components must be finite"

to get [a UI scene pose at] {vector:position} [rotated] {vector:rotation} [scaled] {vector:scale}:
    require finite UI scene vector position
    require finite UI scene vector rotation
    require finite UI scene vector scale
    require condition (((the x of scale) != 0.0) and (((the y of scale) != 0.0) and ((the z of scale) != 0.0))) reporting "Scene poses require nonzero scales"
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI scene pose, the UI scene vector form of position, the UI scene vector form of rotation, the UI scene vector form of scale)

to get [an identity UI scene pose]:
    set origin to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
    set scale to a new vector with x 1.0, y 1.0 and z 1.0
    return a UI scene pose at origin rotated origin scaled scale

to get {UI scene pose:first} [is the same UI scene pose as] {UI scene pose:second}:
    set left to [first's position's x, first's position's y, first's position's z, first's rotation's x, first's rotation's y, first's rotation's z, first's scale's x, first's scale's y, first's scale's z]
    set right to [second's position's x, second's position's y, second's position's z, second's rotation's x, second's rotation's y, second's rotation's z, second's scale's x, second's scale's y, second's scale's z]
    set index to 0
    loop while index < 9:
        if (the item at index in left) != (the item at index in right):
            return false
        increment index
    return true

to get [the UI scene matrix for] {UI scene pose:pose}:
    require finite UI scene vector (pose's position)
    require finite UI scene vector (pose's rotation)
    require finite UI scene vector (pose's scale)
    set x to pose's rotation's x
    set y to pose's rotation's y
    set z to pose's rotation's z
    set a to the cosine of x
    set b to the sine of x
    set c to the cosine of y
    set d to the sine of y
    set e to the cosine of z
    set f to the sine of z
    set matrix to an identity graphics matrix
    store ((c * e * pose's scale's x) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 0
    store (((a * f + b * e * d) * pose's scale's x) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 1
    store (((b * f - a * e * d) * pose's scale's x) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 2
    store (((0.0 - c * f) * pose's scale's y) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 4
    store (((a * e - b * f * d) * pose's scale's y) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 5
    store (((b * e + a * f * d) * pose's scale's y) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 6
    store ((d * pose's scale's z) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 8
    store (((0.0 - b * c) * pose's scale's z) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 9
    store ((a * c * pose's scale's z) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 10
    store (pose's position's x as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 12
    store (pose's position's y as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 13
    store (pose's position's z as a 32 bit floating-point number) into matrix at 14
    return matrix
